  "issue": {
    "author": "JulienKaspar",
    "body_normalized": "**System Information**\nOperating system: Linux-6.18.20-gentoo-dist-x86_64-AMD_Ryzen_Threadripper_1950X_16-Core_Processor-with-glibc2.42 64 Bits, WAYLAND UI\nGraphics card: AMD Radeon RX 7900 XT (RADV NAVI31) Advanced Micro Devices radv Mesa 26.0.4 Vulkan Backend\n\n**Blender Version**\nBroken: version: 5.2.0 Alpha, branch: main, commit date: 2026-04-06 22:56, hash: `0118924432e5`\nBroken: 3.6\n\n**Short description of error**\nI noticed that when I had cavity auto-masking enabled and then decided to create a mask from it with the \"Create Mask\" button, it would actually create an inverted mask. Any vertices that the auto-masking would leave alone to be sculpted on, will be the masked vertices. This seems backwards\n\n**Exact steps for others to reproduce the error**\n- Add a monkey objects, subdivide it a bunch and apply the modifiers\n- Go to sculpt mode\n- Enable Cavity auto-masking in the header and try sculpting with the grab brush\n- Press the \"Create Mask\" button in the auto-masking panel and disable the auto-masking\n- Now try painting on the mesh again -> It's the opposite result.",
    "body_raw": "**System Information**\nOperating system: Linux-6.18.20-gentoo-dist-x86_64-AMD_Ryzen_Threadripper_1950X_16-Core_Processor-with-glibc2.42 64 Bits, WAYLAND UI\nGraphics card: AMD Radeon RX 7900 XT (RADV NAVI31) Advanced Micro Devices radv Mesa 26.0.4 Vulkan Backend\n\n**Blender Version**\nBroken: version: 5.2.0 Alpha, branch: main, commit date: 2026-04-06 22:56, hash: `0118924432e5`\nBroken: 3.6\n\n**Short description of error**\nI noticed that when I had cavity auto-masking enabled and then decided to create a mask from it with the \"Create Mask\" button, it would actually create an inverted mask. Any vertices that the auto-masking would leave alone to be sculpted on, will be the masked vertices. This seems backwards \n\n**Exact steps for others to reproduce the error**\n- Add a monkey objects, subdivide it a bunch and apply the modifiers\n- Go to sculpt mode\n- Enable Cavity auto-masking in the header and try sculpting with the grab brush\n- Press the \"Create Mask\" button in the auto-masking panel and disable the auto-masking\n- Now try painting on the mesh again -> It's the opposite result.\n\n\n",
    "body_sha256": "ef602356907000247447efd2b6e147bfac506cbcb5b52f93bded63dec9b49ade",
